From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:24:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: Keep the link up across system suspend on MSM8996

Since commit 2cc0e7454c ("PCI: qcom: Add D3cold support"), system suspend
powers down the host and vddpe-3v3 whenever the endpoint is in D3hot.

MSM8996 boards feed the whole endpoint from that supply. On the Galaxy Tab
S3 it is WLAN_EN of a QCA6174, and it pulls in the chip's 3.3 V rail, which
the Bluetooth half needs too. The link does not come back on resume, and
Wi-Fi is gone until the next boot:

  qcom-pcie 600000.pcie: Device not found
  ath10k_pci 0000:01:00.0: Unable to change power state from D3hot to D0, device inaccessible

Holding BT_EN low across the suspend does not help. Why the link fails to
train is not understood.

Before that commit the driver kept the host up while the link was up. Do
that again on this controller by skipping the D3cold sequence while a device
is attached, so the endpoint stays powered in D3hot.

Fixes: 2cc0e7454c ("PCI: qcom: Add D3cold support")
Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index b58a607b71..e0d45cb924 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -281,6 +281,7 @@ struct qcom_pcie_cfg {
 	bool override_no_snoop;
 	bool firmware_managed;
 	bool no_l0s;
+	bool no_d3cold;
 };
 
 struct qcom_pcie_perst {
@@ -1612,6 +1613,7 @@ static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_2_1_0 = {
 static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_2_3_2 = {
 	.ops = &ops_2_3_2,
 	.no_l0s = true,
+	.no_d3cold = true,
 };
 
 static const struct qcom_pcie_cfg cfg_2_3_3 = {
@@ -2346,9 +2348,16 @@ static int qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 	if (!pcie)
 		return 0;
 
-	ret = dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(pcie->pci);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * MSM8996 boards power the whole endpoint from vddpe-3v3, often a
+	 * Wi-Fi/Bluetooth combo chip. Cutting it takes Bluetooth down too, and
+	 * on the Galaxy Tab S3 the link does not train again on resume.
+	 */
+	if (!pcie->cfg->no_d3cold || !dw_pcie_link_up(pcie->pci)) {
+		ret = dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(pcie->pci);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	if (pcie->pci->suspended) {
 		ret = icc_disable(pcie->icc_mem);
